{"seq":4,"slug":"maintaining-context-files","title":"Maintaining Context Files","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/project-context-files/maintaining-context-files","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"keeping-context-fresh","title":"保持上下文新鲜","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/project-context-files/maintaining-context-files/keeping-context-fresh","wordCount":2204,"readingTime":9},{"seq":2,"slug":"context-from-recurring-mistakes","title":"从反复出错反推该补什么","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/project-context-files/maintaining-context-files/context-from-recurring-mistakes","wordCount":1985,"readingTime":8},{"seq":3,"slug":"context-as-living-doc","title":"把上下文当活文档","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-native-engineering/project-context-files/maintaining-context-files/context-as-living-doc","wordCount":1840,"readingTime":8}],"introMarkdown":"本章讲上下文文件写完之后怎么不让它烂掉。上下文文件会过期——项目变了它没变,过期的上下文比没有更糟,因为它会理直气壮地误导 agent(照着早已不存在的命令、约定去做)。保持新鲜:把更新上下文当成改动的一部分(改了命令/约定/结构就同步改上下文),而非事后才想起。从反复出错反推该补什么:agent(和人)反复猜错、反复踩的同一个坑、反复问的同一件事,正是上下文该补或该改的最高信号——把错误当成上下文的待办清单。最终把上下文当活文档:它和代码一样是项目的一等资产,要持续小步维护、随项目一起演进,而非写一次就供着。\n"}